    "body": "### Problem\n\nSvelteKit uses parenthesized/bracketed directory names. If I try to `:e` one of these on Windows, tab completion fails because it is interpreting `\\(` as an escaped parenthesis instead of a dir separator. It autocompletes the parenthesized directory, but the parenthesis need to be escaped manually, otherwise it will open the wrong (nonexistent) file. If I escape the name manually and then press tab, it will remove the backslashes, so to edit one of these SvelteKit files I have to type the entire path without autocompletion.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nPowerShell / nvim:\n```\nmkdir \"foo\\(bar)\"\necho test > \"foo\\(bar)\\baz.txt\"\nnvim\n:e foo\\ <press tab>\n:e foo\\\\(bar\\)\\ <press tab>\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nCompletion should automatically escape the parenthesis. It looks like `[]` don't need to be escaped, but it won't autocomplete past a directory with those in the name either.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.12.6\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNo, vim 9.2.0000. Vim doesn't autocomplete, but does need the ()'s escaped.\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nWindows 11 26H2\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nWindows Terminal 1.25.2733\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nDoesn't apply on Windows\n\n### Installation\n\nwinget",
